AB  - This paper proposes a federated learning-based framework specifically designed for privacy-preserving data analytics in 6G networks. Federated learning enables data to remain local on edge devices while only transmitting model updates, ensuring sensitive user data is not exposed. Our experimental results demonstrate that this framework not only maintains high privacy standards but also improves the speed and accuracy of data analytics when compared to traditional centralized methods. The proposed framework addresses the privacy challenges of handling vast, heterogeneous data in 6G environments. By enhancing privacy preservation and processing efficiency, federated learning is positioned as a critical enabler for next-generation networks.
ER  - 

