AB  - This paper presents the design, implementation, and experimental evaluation of a new concept for a multi-drone system capable of executing complex aerial missions in both indoor and outdoor environments. The novelty of the proposed architecture consists in integrating ultra-wideband communication, onboard Artificial Intelligence (AI) for object detection, and a web-based control interface to coordinate multiple microdrones of the type Crazyflie 2.1. Key functionalities include real-time video surveillance, autonomous navigation to predefined coordinates, precise indoor positioning using Time Difference of Arrival (TDoA), optical flow-based stability, and onboard object detection. Experimental results demonstrate the system's robustness, adaptability, and potential for real-world applications such as security monitoring, industrial inspection, and intelligent autonomous operations in GPS-denied environments.
