AB  - Resource allocation has a significant impact on the efficiency of vehicle-to-everything (V2X) networks. In order to achieve efficient resource allocation, this paper presents a novel Event-Triggered Federated Reinforcement Learning (ETFRL) scheme. This scheme modifies the Multi-Agent Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (MADDPG) scheme to enable agents to be aware of global interference, thereby optimizing overall network performance. Furthermore, the model integrates Federated Learning (FL) to protect user data privacy and accelerate training speed. It also incorporates an Event-Triggered mechanism to selectively initiate the Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) process, reducing the training burden. Simulation results demonstrate that the ETFRL scheme achieves near-equivalent performance to the time-triggered algorithm while significantly reducing execution times. This indicates that the ETFRL scheme is a promising approach for enhancing spectrum efficiency in V2X resource allocation problem.
ER  - 

