AB  - This research examines the critical challenges and technical requirements of communication systems for first responders, including law enforcement, fire services, and emergency medical services (EMS). It identifies limitations in current systems, such as interoperability barriers, outdated radio infrastructure, and inadequate real-time data integration. Emerging technologies, including IoT-enabled autonomous vehicles (AVs), 5G communication networks, and Vehicle-to-Everything (V2X) protocols, are analyzed for their potential to address these issues. These advancements offer enhanced real-time geolocation accuracy, improved situational awareness, and seamless multi-agency information exchange. The findings highlight key technical obstacles and provide insights into how innovative solutions can enhance the operational efficiency, reliability, and safety of first responder communication systems.
